# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — contract

<!-- trailhead v{{VERSION}} -->

**This file states what must be true. It does not track where the work is.**

That lives in `.planning/STATE.md`. The separation is the point: a document edited every
deliverable stops being an authority, because its claims drift while the prose around
them stays accurate. If you find yourself adding a status column here, you are writing
STATE.md in the wrong file.

**Amend, don't edit.** Changing an invariant is a decision with consequences upstream and
down. Add a dated amendment section at the bottom rather than rewriting the line, so the
change is visible in a diff and reviewable as a change rather than as prose that has
always said this.

**Keep it under {{CONTRACT_LINE_CAP}} lines.** Past that, nobody reads it, and an unread
contract is worse than none — it gives the appearance of governance while providing none.
If it is growing, that is usually state or rationale trying to live here; move state to
`.planning/STATE.md` and rationale to the decision log.

